{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1000110-espionage-how-to-play-a-guardian-or-seers-in-2e","id":1000110,"title":"Espionage - How to play a Guardian or Seers in 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-07T20:20:26-08:00","id":1000110,"title":"Espionage - How to play a Guardian or Seers in 2e","content":"So I am running a game in which one of my players plays a guardian who is dead set on basically no one but guardians knowing who he is. He consistently uses cloaking magic to keep his magic hidden, and always wears disguises when dealing with mages. (All Mages, mind.) Recently he's realized that secrecy becomes incredibly difficult when dealing with... well, any Obrimos or anyone with a remote knowledge of prime, due to Pierce Deception. It makes it hard for him to be as secretive as he likes, when the fact that he IS so fake causes people to actually be more interested in him than if he hadn't used magic at all to hide himself.<br /> <br /> Reading through it, mages in 2e are incredibly good at picking up and discerning the truth of a situation. It's nearly impossibly to deceive most mages. So this brought up a question - how would a Guardian, Seer, or any other character manage to infiltrate another cabal or order - how does espionage work, when 1/5th of mages can cut through lies like butter, and when efforts to go hidden invoke clashes - (which other mages recognize this happening, as all mages know when their spells clash) - which in turn invoke further investigation? <br /> <br /> I'm finding it a challenge to discern this, and knowing this kind of thing is important to him I'd like to figure out how it would be done in this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T20:35:08-08:00","id":1000116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1000110-espionage-how-to-play-a-guardian-or-seers-in-2e#post1000110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes it hard for him to be as secretive as he likes, when the fact that he IS so fake causes people to actually be more interested in him than if he hadn't used magic at all to hide himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that playing out tradecraft is fun for a lot of players, but this image is just really funny to me.<br /> <br /> Has he tried...acting casual? One option, especially with spells like Pierce Deception, would be mundanely finding ways to speak and present yourself that aren't actually lies.<br /> <br /> Establishing social convention against investigation spells as part of the setting is one option. One of my own PCs is averse to using spells like Pierce Deception or Read the Depths because she sees it as rude/aggressive, maybe you could make that common and have NPCs be slow to magically verify things because it's seen as insulting. Or conversely, establish in the setting that it's common for mages to use secrecy and misdirection in person, so seeing that someone has a Veiling spell up isn't a huge red flag because many mages do that.<br /> <br /> Maybe he could use Memory Hole to forget incriminating information when it's not relevant. He doesn't even consciously know he's lying.<br /> <br /> In 1E the Seers were written as heavily using Profane Urim artifacts to possess people and use them as proxies, maybe you could adapt that and make the Artifact effect less obvious than a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T21:01:59-08:00","id":1000126,"title":"","content":"I think your Guardian's problem can be solved by their Order-specific Merit, Masque. It allows you to change your Signature Nimbus, change your Virtue and Vice, basically change everything that could easily identify you to Supernal Magic. It also allows you to pad out your identity with Social Merits explicit to that identity, if memory serves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T01:49:59-08:00","id":1000189,"title":"","content":"In the Guardian book there's a section that deals with how Guardians talk in code in order to talk about sensitive measures in public. It could of easily be used as an obfuscation technique in general, coming up with a personal lingo for talking about stuff that other Mages won't quickly comprehend and changing the lingo's vocabulary frequently to avoid pattern building that could be used to crack it.<br /> <br /> Also, if he knows enough Prime to cloak himself then he also knows enough Prime to Counterspell. It wouldn't be out of place for that to be his knee jerk reaction to spells cast in his presence that he hasn't been warned are coming. Not saying what your intentions are when you cast with someone not in your cabal is kind of rude since any spell could be a death sentence. That's why Mages follow the Rites and stuff, to try and add a level of predictability that's hard to come by.<br /> <br /> Then there's Masques, and there are legacies that are very good at infiltration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T02:56:57-08:00","id":1000196,"title":"","content":"Well I've always relied upon component Sleeper and Sleepwalker spy networks for espionage in my Mage Chronicles. Both the Guardians and the Seers primarily use these networks (both vastly different morally and aesthetically) to spy on rivals and their mortal followers, only relying upon direct espionage under the most necessary of circumstances. When they do have to 007 mingle the Guardians have it easiest thanks to the Masques, but all Mages can use their Shadow Names to good effect when it comes to resonance and nimbus (if I'm remembering nimbus correctly it changes depending upon one's Shadow Name.) Other than that, for interactions with their Cabal, Order, or Consili I use the basic social contract of not using magic on fellow Awakened to discourage players from using detection on every single other Mage or potential Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T04:01:18-08:00","id":1000207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1000110-espionage-how-to-play-a-guardian-or-seers-in-2e?p=1000189#post1000189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Guardian book there's a section that deals with how Guardians talk in code in order to talk about sensitive measures in public. It could of easily be used as an obfuscation technique in general, coming up with a personal lingo for talking about stuff that other Mages won't quickly comprehend and changing the lingo's vocabulary frequently to avoid pattern building that could be used to crack it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was flipping through Immortals last night and there's a one-dot 'Cultural Language' merit to represent those private languages.<br /> <br /> I think the vital element to using those codes is also to, as Caladriu said, act casual. Any Mind Disciple can use Universal Language to crack the code instantly but they need to know there's a code there in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T06:52:47-08:00","id":1000249,"title":"","content":"You can also go with way of Pink from <b>Vampire the Masquerade Redemption</b> - He is rebellious modern Brujah...<br /> (See clip from 5:35 )<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VxmmRPISFNU\" data-code=\"VxmmRPISFNU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VxmmRPISFNU/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> To be later unveiled being Assamite, all along! </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> (See from 24:57 now )<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kSQ9sibEyww\" data-code=\"kSQ9sibEyww\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/kSQ9sibEyww/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> In the nutshell - <b>You are true to telling you are Awakened. You only change Order and/or Path you are showing to others.</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T06:59:23-08:00","id":1000251,"title":"","content":"Something else worth remembering is that Mages don't use spells like Pierce Deception <i>constantly</i>. I've got a Thyrsus character who is theoretically impossible to sneak up on - a Life Knowing spell to detect anything larger than a rabbit inside a city-block-sized radius makes you downright nearly omniscient when it comes to humans - but that spell isn't going to always be active. At best, it's merely infuriatingly distracting; at worst, it leads to violations of the Veil.<br /> <br /> Another thing worth remembering is that Mages can use &quot;deep&quot; spells and techniques to alter their minds and memories in the event they do need to pass just such a magical test. Delving into your Oneiros and symbolically sealing away everything that is not the false identity and giving yourself a key to unlock it again will leave not even <i>you</i> remembering who you really are until later is one such option.<br /> <br /> Others have given good tips too. Most notably, where there's no smoke, there's no fire: A Mage who doesn't make a lot of obvious effort at hiding something won't attract the curiosity of people whose existence is defined by seeking out what's hidden. The best secret identity is one no-one even suspects is secret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T07:01:40-08:00","id":1000253,"title":"","content":"Play act as other mage - change Order you officially work for and assume False Shadow Name. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T07:45:02-08:00","id":1000267,"title":"","content":"Another way to throw off Mages is to play on their preconceptions, take up one obvious kind of behavior that's attention getting and is meant to &quot;mask&quot; something else. For instance, maybe your character sneaks off to the bathroom a lot, suspiciously often. Another Mage looking into it finds out more often than not is actually sneaking out for a smoke break. Mystery solved. Once that layer is set up as long as you consistently maintain that activity you can occasionally use your &quot;bathroom break&quot; nee &quot;smoke break&quot; to do something more covert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T02:05:42-08:00","id":1000668,"title":"","content":"Another (and very fun) option is to have several layers of disguise. For example, having an imbued item (a mask) to conceal your face when dealing your mages, and getting very offended if one mage try to peer across. Under the mask (that would provoke a Clash of Wills), put other cloaking spell. Even if the mage in question wins the Clash of Wills, he would see the other cover. And before he tries (again), you can challenge him to Duel Arcane, <i>at least</i>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11688-marciano666","name":"marciano666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T05:18:07-08:00","id":1000711,"title":"","content":"My first suggestion - watch Burn Notice. Seriously, that is an awesome show for inspiration on playing a spy in the CofD.<br /> <br /> Anyways. So, you will want to focus on Masques for your fake cover identit(ies), at minimum 3 dots. Nimbus identity via scrutiny needs to be avoided at all cost. Otherwise, everything else is meaningless. Use magic to help reinforce that role - use Mind to rewrite your own memories, and claim that you're doing the whole curse-self-for-enlightenment that's supposed to be a thing. That way, you won't be telling lies. Use life magic to alter your appearance through Lasting effects like growing out your hair. Posture and attitude go a long way after that. And they're not disguises, so they can't be pierced.<br /> <br /> After that? The key is working an angle so that people don't -question- you in the first place. Use socialize and subterfuge to blend in. You want to be a chameleon, not a shadow. You're already taking a Masque to hide yourself, so pick a role that's unobtrusive. The key is to act in a way that doesn't invite scruntiny. Mages excel at information gathering. You will not beat them at that if they want to try anything and everything. So, you don't. Hide things in plain sight, not shadows.<br /> <br /> There's a few Legacies suitable for spies - Legion for one. Working on that may help as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> To infiltrate an Order, you'll have to adopt a personality that resonates with that Order, make it seem like you're a good recruit, and slip in as a low member recruit. Work your way up normally. Undercover operations tend to be long term, so he's going to have to work at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T07:41:11-08:00","id":1000781,"title":"","content":"Advice I'm about to give is setting dependent. It will work best if the following is true: Mages maintain relatively large support cast of Sleepwalker and Sleeper followers, and these auxiliary organizations and structures outnumber actual Mages.<br /> <br /> If your Magical Society relies on these non-magical members to do stuff and things, infiltrating actual Inner Enlightened Circles is very dangerous and relatively high risk low reward thing. It's much safer and easier to interact with Sleeper minions; while these minions usually lack perspective to understand information and task they are given, you as a Mage will probably have means to connect the dots, identify patterns and generally, paint bigger picture using information gathered from these support organizations. Lay low, avoid and minimize contact with actual Enemy Mages. Use your magic to conceal yourself, try to pass as a Sleeper, use your magic to extract information from minions and conceal your tracks. Be prepared to abort the operation at any time. Never invite scrutiny. Magic is amazing at gathering information. Infiltrating Order as a Mage without heavy Prime and Masque investment is borderline suicidal. Rely on magic only when absolutely needed, master some mundane skills, especially the deception oriented ones. Be prepared to operate on no Mana whatsoever, as while you can hide your Awakened Nature by smart use of Prime, Death or Mind spells, it would be very embarassing to be caught by someone accidentally noticing that you possess Mage-like Mana in your Pattern.<br /> <br /> And of course, if everything fails, try to make a deal and become a double spy. Better that than dead. Don't approach being discovered as a death sentence; think of it more like a business opportunity for everyone involved, including your initial bosses. Death spy is of no use for anyone, discovered spy potentially is useful for everyone. So, plan for being caught, and have some prepwork for a deal already done. In fact, sometimes it might be useful to identify a greedy party in the enemy structure, reveal yourself to them at purpose, and become their pawn in exchange for protection and better insider backing. If you become a double agent employed by a greedy Seer, you might do more good for the Pentacle by helping his schemes and providing him with information he needs in exchange for ability to strike at his political opponents easier; if you can estabilish a foothold in enemy organization, do it. Information that will lead to death of 3 Pentacle Mages might sound like a price too harsh to pay, but that's your job as a Guardian. Sacrifice some, save many.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> As for &quot;actually layering yourself with literally fortresses and walls of magical protection to hide yourself&quot; - my head of the Guardians was something like that. Always appearing in enchanted full body armor, with layers of spells obfuscating their presence, with history and sympathetic links erased to the ground. Basicall, a faceless, armored juggernaut of magical might. Tons of rumors and stories. Very scary. You don't want to cross that guy. <br /> <br /> The Thing was that there wasn't really a &quot;Guardian Councilor of Doom&quot;. Armor was real, and heavily enchanted to look scary and provide a really hard to crack mess of spells, but it was it. No real Bigger Than Life evil overlord figure. Highest ranking Guardian members all had a Masque dedicated to being the Overlord, and they rotated who is actually wearing the armor during big events. It was mostly for misdirection purposes and to create a big target; people were either intimidated by &quot;raw brute force&quot; of the Overlord, or they felt challenged by his incredible mystery. And well...if there is no real person inside, there is no truth to be discovered.<br /> So basically our Guardians created a scapegoat to be hated, which allowed one of their key members to be seen as a abused and trying-to-do-it-right guy in conflict with evil overseer and someone &quot;to go when you need to deal with Guardians and don't want to attract attention of the more radical guys&quot;.<br /> Basically, they created fire so big that they all were hiding in his shadows, without actually using much magic or subterfuge. Just...redirecting attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 11-09-2016, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-16T06:30:25-08:00","id":1018044,"title":"","content":"It's true that mages are very good at discerning the truth -- <i>after they discover the presence of misdirection.</i><br /> <br /> In my Reign of the Exarch chronicles, the party fell prey to entirely mundane spying techniques. They assumed a mage spying on them would ping their PMS; when ultimately a simple tape recorder hidden in their house was enough. For several weeks. They never noticed it was there.<br /> <br /> The trick to Mage espionage is not giving your targets a reason to suspect you in the first place. Ultimately, this is the trick to all espionage, but it's especially true in the world of Mage, where facts can be learned with the snap of a finger. You should focus less on defeating investigation, and more on not inspiring it to start with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T05:51:39-08:00","id":1023211,"title":"","content":"Espionage in mage 101: Don't rely in magical means to do it. It's relatively easy, but it's like having a script-kiddie trying to access the Pentagon database. Tech is 100% more reliable than anything else - bugs, mics and wireless cameras don't suffer soul-scarring and mind-bending damage for fulfilling their purpose, and if you catch people screwing with the lex you have evidence of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}